WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.122 --> 00:00:19.664
wish Little Spot had turned out to be the thief after all," Maggie said with a sigh.

2
00:00:19.684 --> 00:00:22.966
"Then the mystery would be solved.

3
00:00:24.166 --> 00:00:27.728
And I wouldn't still be worried that Mom and Dad are going to make me stop riding."

4
00:00:28.876 --> 00:00:33.458
Henry, Cole, and Maggie were at the lemonade stand talking about what had happened yesterday.

5
00:00:33.478 --> 00:00:38.020
"We thought Little Spot was guilty at first," Cole said.

6
00:00:38.040 --> 00:00:41.361
"But then Henry started thinking logically again."

7
00:00:42.402 --> 00:00:43.282
Henry smiled.

8
00:00:43.302 --> 00:00:48.124
"Little Spot did grab your sandal," he reminded Maggie.

9
00:00:48.144 --> 00:00:50.505
"But then I thought of something.

10
00:00:51.626 --> 00:00:54.467
Why would a dog steal things only from you?

11
00:00:54.487 --> 00:00:56.708
It didn't make sense.

12
00:00:57.844 --> 00:01:00.266
The other riders leave their stuff sitting around too."

13
00:01:00.286 --> 00:01:05.289
"That's why we questioned everyone after your lesson," Cole went on.

14
00:01:05.309 --> 00:01:09.713
"We wanted to make sure the thief wasn't stealing stuff from everyone."

15
00:01:10.994 --> 00:01:13.515
"Nobody else is missing anything," Henry said.

16
00:01:13.535 --> 00:01:15.897
"Well, except for Ms.

17
00:01:15.937 --> 00:01:18.399
Wood." Cole nodded.

18
00:01:18.419 --> 00:01:22.362
"She said the barn cat's bed has been missing for a few days.

19
00:01:23.462 --> 00:01:25.484
But she's pretty sure a raccoon took that."

20
00:01:26.420 --> 00:01:31.865
"We also did an experiment to see if Little Spot would try to grab anything else," Henry said.

21
00:01:31.885 --> 00:01:34.166
"We used Cole's sock.

22
00:01:35.267 --> 00:01:37.869
Little Spot sniffed it, but he didn't pick it up."

23
00:01:37.889 --> 00:01:42.953
"So we decided that Little Spot just likes to grab shoes," Cole said.

24
00:01:42.973 --> 00:01:48.598
"My neighbor's dog is the same way, except he only steals TV remote controls."

25
00:01:49.779 --> 00:01:50.820
Maggie sighed again.

26
00:01:50.840 --> 00:01:55.924
"Well, it definitely wasn't Big Spot either," she said.

27
00:01:56.960 --> 00:01:58.842
"He might have been able to grab my sock.

28
00:01:59.823 --> 00:02:01.584
But he couldn't have taken my bracelet.

29
00:02:02.665 --> 00:02:06.228
I put it in my bag as I led him out, and it was missing as soon as

30
00:02:06.288 --> 00:02:06.989
I got back."

31
00:02:08.570 --> 00:02:14.395
"Really? Then I guess we can rule out all of the animal suspects," Henry said.

32
00:02:15.476 --> 00:02:16.216
Cole laughed.

33
00:02:16.236 --> 00:02:21.000
"Yeah. The barn cat couldn't have picked up your grooming brush."

34
00:02:21.020 --> 00:02:24.083
"So who are our human suspects?"

35
00:02:24.523 --> 00:02:25.264
Maggie asked.

36
00:02:26.336 --> 00:02:29.057
"All the other riders in your class," Henry said.

37
00:02:29.077 --> 00:02:30.877
"Plus Jill."

38
00:02:32.338 --> 00:02:33.558
"Right," Cole said.

39
00:02:33.578 --> 00:02:37.899
"We found out that Jill wishes she had more money for riding.

40
00:02:39.080 --> 00:02:41.540
What if she stole your stuff so she could sell it?"

41
00:02:41.560 --> 00:02:44.221
"Who would buy one sock?"

42
00:02:44.701 --> 00:02:45.501
Maggie asked.

43
00:02:46.722 --> 00:02:48.442
"Nobody," Henry answered.

44
00:02:48.462 --> 00:02:52.563
"We figured you might have lost that on your way into the barn."

45
00:02:54.124 --> 00:02:54.984
Maggie frowned.

46
00:02:56.044 --> 00:02:57.665
"You're as bad as my parents!

47
00:02:58.826 --> 00:03:00.387
I didn't lose that sock.

48
00:03:01.527 --> 00:03:04.109
I know it was in my bag when I put the bag down!"

49
00:03:05.349 --> 00:03:06.510
Henry wasn't so sure.

50
00:03:07.671 --> 00:03:11.493
He still didn't think Maggie was careless enough to lose the check or the other stuff.

51
00:03:12.633 --> 00:03:17.516
But it would be easy for her to drop a sock without noticing, especially when she was excited

52
00:03:17.556 --> 00:03:18.557
about going riding.

53
00:03:20.258 --> 00:03:21.438
He didn't say that though.

54
00:03:22.499 --> 00:03:24.260
He didn't want to make Maggie angry.

55
00:03:25.420 --> 00:03:27.121
"How well do you know Eleanor?"

56
00:03:27.441 --> 00:03:28.542
he asked instead.

57
00:03:28.562 --> 00:03:30.583
"Not that well."

58
00:03:31.003 --> 00:03:31.784
Maggie shrugged.

59
00:03:31.804 --> 00:03:34.625
"We've only had four lessons together.

60
00:03:35.666 --> 00:03:37.026
But I doubt she's the thief."

61
00:03:38.167 --> 00:03:39.508
"Why?" Cole asked.

62
00:03:39.528 --> 00:03:42.409
"You just said you don't know her very well.

63
00:03:43.490 --> 00:03:45.091
How do you know she's not sneaky?"

64
00:03:45.111 --> 00:03:49.793
"Because she takes such good care of her dog," Maggie said.

65
00:03:49.813 --> 00:03:54.316
"She's just as crazy about Little Spot as I am about my kittens.

66
00:03:55.568 --> 00:03:57.650
Someone like that has to be a good person."

67
00:03:57.670 --> 00:04:00.332
"Okay," Henry said.

68
00:04:00.352 --> 00:04:02.694
"But what about the others?

69
00:04:03.815 --> 00:04:06.818
We noticed Daisy was acting kind of competitive."

70
00:04:07.878 --> 00:04:09.360
"Yeah, she's always like that."

71
00:04:10.380 --> 00:04:11.481
Maggie rolled her eyes.

72
00:04:11.501 --> 00:04:14.864
"She wants to try everything first.

73
00:04:15.965 --> 00:04:17.907
And she thinks she's the best at whatever we do."

74
00:04:17.927 --> 00:04:21.189
"Then there's Zach," Cole said.

75
00:04:21.209 --> 00:04:24.072
"He was complaining about everything.

76
00:04:24.992 --> 00:04:27.413
What if he's stealing stuff because he hates riding?"

77
00:04:28.374 --> 00:04:32.315
"I still think his sister, Jill, is a better suspect," Henry said.

78
00:04:32.335 --> 00:04:34.656
"She has the best motive.

79
00:04:35.637 --> 00:04:36.477
She needs money."

80
00:04:36.497 --> 00:04:38.898
"I agree, Henry.

81
00:04:39.958 --> 00:04:41.379
But here come some customers."

82
00:04:42.600 --> 00:04:45.701
Maggie pointed to several people heading toward the lemonade stand.

83
00:04:46.701 --> 00:04:48.662
"We'll have to finish talking about this later."

84
00:04:48.682 --> 00:04:52.724
"I hope we can solve the mystery today," Maggie said.

85
00:04:53.780 --> 00:04:56.882
"Otherwise Mom said this might be my last lesson for a while."

86
00:04:58.384 --> 00:04:59.364
She sounded upset.

87
00:05:00.365 --> 00:05:01.446
Henry didn't blame her.

88
00:05:05.249 --> 00:05:08.871
It was a few days later, and The Lemonade Detectives were back at the barn.

89
00:05:08.891 --> 00:05:11.733
"Do you have both of your socks today?"

90
00:05:12.094 --> 00:05:12.874
Cole asked.

91
00:05:13.955 --> 00:05:15.196
Maggie made a face at him.

92
00:05:15.216 --> 00:05:20.180
"You already asked me that twenty times," she said.

93
00:05:21.256 --> 00:05:23.658
"I told you, I stuck them in my boots today.

94
00:05:24.678 --> 00:05:26.480
There's no way they can fall out."

95
00:05:27.460 --> 00:05:28.461
Henry noticed Ms.

96
00:05:28.501 --> 00:05:29.762
Wood hurrying toward them.

97
00:05:30.843 --> 00:05:33.424
The barn owner had an anxious expression on her face.

98
00:05:34.605 --> 00:05:35.666
"Maggie!" Ms.

99
00:05:35.726 --> 00:05:36.366
Wood said.

100
00:05:36.386 --> 00:05:38.448
"There you are.

101
00:05:38.608 --> 00:05:41.490
I need to speak with you about something serious."

102
00:05:41.510 --> 00:05:43.832
"I'm not late, am I?"

103
00:05:44.252 --> 00:05:45.052
Maggie asked.

104
00:05:46.173 --> 00:05:47.314
Ms. Wood shook her head.

105
00:05:47.334 --> 00:05:50.036
"It's not that," she said.

106
00:05:51.104 --> 00:05:52.027
"We have a problem.

107
00:05:53.030 --> 00:05:59.527
Right after you left the barn the other day, I realized something: Big Spot's saddle pad is missing!"
